    "q-74834": {
      "dom_id": "step-q74834",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-4y=-1 \\\\  & 2x-7y=0 \\\\  & -4x+15y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The system is consistent independent\n\nII. The system has no solution\n\nIII. The system is consistent dependent",
      "worked_solution": "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 15 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince any numbers $x$ and $y$ are solutions to the third equation $0x+0y=0$, we can remove this equation from the system. So, the corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-4y=-1 \\\\ y=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we have $y=2$ and substituting this into the first equation yields $x=7.$ So,  we conclude that the system is consistent independent. \n\nAs a result, only statement I is true.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
